      "text": "McFadden (1974 foundational work; 2000 Nobel Prize) formalized mode choice as utility maximization with unobserved heterogeneity. Each mode has an indirect utility — the traveler chooses the mode with highest utility — but since the analyst cannot observe all factors, the choice appears probabilistic."
